     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Hi everyone,</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Can someone help me with this?</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> I placed my\r\nlandmarks with Landmark Editor and export as .dta for process in RStudio, so</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">I tried to </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">use the estimate.missing of geomorph package and\r\nshow this error message</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"background:white;margin:0px;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\">Error in gpagen(A[, , -spec.NA], PrinAxes = FALSE, print.progress\r\n= FALSE) : </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"background:white;margin:0px;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt\"><span style=\"margin:0px\">  </span>Coordinates\r\narray does not have proper dimensions</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">I also tried to use the package ‘LOST’</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">(J. Arbour and C. Brown)</span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> for align and estimate some missing\r\ndata in my dataset, however, the R studio shows these error messages:</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"background:white;margin:0px;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Error in </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black\"><a href=\"http://aligned.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aligned.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484802941000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2PusJhVkG9vT_MY2WnwpgU\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(17,85,204);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><u>aligned.com</u></span></a></span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">[ ,y, ] : subscript out of bounds</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"background:white;margin:0px;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">o</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">r</span><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"background:white;margin:0px;line-height:normal;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Error in </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black\"><a href=\"http://aligned.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aligned.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484802941000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2PusJhVkG9vT_MY2WnwpgU\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\" style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(17,85,204);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"><u>aligned.com</u></span></a></span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">[, , z] : subscript out of bounds</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">any idea what might be going on or what I&#39;m doing wrong?</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"> ^^</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin:0px;line-height:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"margin:0px;color:black;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Thanks in advance,</span><span style=\"margin:0px;color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>"
