     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Leonardo Lobo<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Monday, August 26, 2019 6:07 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> geomorph R package &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geomorph-...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [geomorph-r-package] help with missing data in dta file<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hi everyone,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Can someone help me with this? I placed my landmarks with Landmark Editor and export as .dta for process in RStudio, so I tried to use the\r\n estimate.missing of geomorph package and show this error message</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Error in gpagen(A[, , -spec.NA], PrinAxes = FALSE, print.progress = FALSE) :\r\n</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">  Coordinates array does not have proper dimensions</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I also tried to use the package ‘LOST’ (J. Arbour and C. Brown) for align and estimate some missing data in my dataset, however, the R studio\r\n shows these error messages:</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#c5060b\">Error in\r\n</span><span style=\"color:black\"><a href=\"http://aligned.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aligned.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484802945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jcENHrdJnq0b9OB_VetA4\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1155cc\">aligned.com</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#c5060b\">[\r\n ,y, ] : subscript out of bounds</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#222222\">o</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">r</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt;background:white;word-break:break-all\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#c5060b\">Error in\r\n</span><span style=\"color:black\"><a href=\"http://aligned.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aligned.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792484802945000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2jcENHrdJnq0b9OB_VetA4\"><span lang=\"PT-BR\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1155cc\">aligned.com</span></a></span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:#c5060b\">[,\r\n , z] : subscript out of bounds</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">any idea what might be going on or what I&#39;m doing wrong? ^^</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Thanks in advance,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
